`decode_table(text, delimiter=",")` parses delimited text using Python's standard CSV quoting rules. Both arguments must be strings, and the delimiter must contain exactly one character; raise `TypeError` or `ValueError` accordingly. Ignore physically blank lines and rows whose cells are all whitespace. Return `[]` if no nonblank rows remain. Every retained row must have the same number of cells as the first retained row; otherwise raise `ValueError`. Malformed CSV quoting must also raise `ValueError`. Preserve cell text exactly, including surrounding whitespace, and return independent row lists.

